    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Security-Officers--per-diem-_R1596": {
      "title": "Security Officers (per diem)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nSaint Anselm College, a private, liberal arts college in the Benedictine tradition, is seeking multiple part-time, per diem Safety and Security Officers to cover special events at the College.  Work assignments will be as needed.  Responsibilities include ensuring the safety of the college community by providing emergency services, campus patrol, securing buildings, facilitating traffic flow and enforcing parking regulations. Qualifications Successful candidates will be detail oriented, honest, dependable and flexible. He or she will possess excellent interpersonal and decision-making skills, as well as, inherent good judgment and writing ability.  High school education required plus two to three years of relevant experience along with one year of security or law enforcement related training; Associates Degree is preferred. Must be able to deal effectively with a wide range of individuals with ability to handle emergency situations calmly and efficiently; valid driver’s license is also required. As the department operates 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, he or she must be available to work nights, weekends, holidays and alternate shifts when necessary. Weekend hours may be required. Successful candidates will be able to assist the college to further its strategic goals for institution-wide diversity and inclusiveness."
    },
    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Admissions-Counselor_R1607": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSaint Anselm College, a private, liberal arts college in the Benedictine tradition, is seeking a full-time, year-round Admission Counselor to join the College’s Admission office.  Reporting to the Associate Director of Admission, the Admission Counselor will be responsible for:  Representing Saint Anselm College to a wide and diverse audience in high schools and at college fair programs Plan, manage, and execute recruitment travel which includes about 8-10 weeks in the fall and 4-5 weeks in the spring Establish and cultivate relationships with secondary school counselors Correspond with prospective students and their families daily Conduct on-campus and off-campus information sessions Participate fully in the evaluation of applications and selection of the incoming class Contribute to the College’s commitment to diversity, equity and inclusion Other duties and responsibilities may be assigned by the Director of Admission Bachelor's degree is required and one to two years of relevant experience working in college admission is preferred. The successful candidate will possess an understanding of and appreciation for the strengths of an undergraduate liberal arts education in the Catholic tradition; self-motivated and independent critical thinker and worker; problem-solving capabilities; solid work ethic; strong oral and written communication skills, including excellent public speaking skills; possess a valid driver's license.   The ability to travel and work nights and weekends is required. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. The successful candidate will be able to assist the College to further its strategic goals for institution-wide diversity. The start time for this position is on or around Tuesday, September 8, 2026. Successful candidates will be able to assist the college in advancing its Catholic identity and strategic priorities, which include institution-wide diversity and inclusiveness."
    },
    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Research-Technician--Department-of-Psychology_R1603-1": {
      "title": "Research Technician, Department of Psychology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Psychology Department at Saint Anselm College seeks a laboratory technician to fill a part-time position for the 2026-2027 academic year (20-25 hours per week/32 weeks per year) to assist in the implementation and maintenance of research labs. Duties will include: maintaining and administering a human subject pool program for use by our majors and department faculty creating and conducting laboratory modules for a rotating selection of research method courses coordination and maintenance of computer hardware and software for observational data, psychophysiological measures, and reaction time studies updating and providing student training for such equipment (e.g., eye tracker) creating and maintaining a database of measures (e.g., surveys, cognitive tests) for student research projects ordering and maintaining supplies for laboratory modules Requirements Bachelor's degree required. Must be computer-literate and have a working knowledge of a statistical software such as SPSS, JASP, SAS, as well as creating surveys such as using Qualtrics or Google forms. Successful applicants will have additional experience or willingness to learn Unreal, Unity Engines, or managing developer identities in game design programs. Please submit letter of intent, resume, and names of references along with contact information via this web site to the attention of Dr. Elizbeth Rickenbach, Chair, Department of Psychology. A transcript indicating completion of the undergraduate degree will also be required. Successful candidates will be able to assist the college to further its strategic goals for institution-wide diversity and inclusiveness ."
    },
    "https://anselm.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Saint-Anselm-College-Campus/Housekeeper-Custodian_R1538": {
      "title": "Housekeeper/Custodian",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-14\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSaint Anselm College, a private, liberal arts college in the Benedictine tradition, has immediate openings for full-time (40 hours per week) custodians/housekeepers. The typical work schedule is Monday-Friday 7 am – 3:30 pm with occasional Saturdays and potential over time.  Duties involve general cleaning of an assigned campus building and event set-ups. Applicants should have the ability to lift heavy equipment such as a vacuum cleaner or floor buffer (l5-30 lbs.).  Must have the ability to understand and follow written instructions, chemical labels and warnings. High school education desirable. General knowledge and skills related to routine housekeeping with commercial/institutional cleaning experience desirable. Related experience in similar workplace setting a plus. Successful candidates will be able to assist the college to further its strategic goals for institution-wide diversity and inclusiveness ."
    }
